 <woodyst@gmail.com>
Date: Sun, 19 Jul 2026 21:33:53 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 063/106] arm64: dts: qcom: sm7150-xiaomi-common: the Bluetooth
 chip is a wcn3990

It is declared as a wcn3998, which is not what these phones carry: the chip
reports ROM version 0x0201 and the factory BTFM partition ships
crbtfw21.tlv / crnv21.bin for it.

The compatible picks the rom_ver formula in btqca.c, and the wcn3998 one -
((soc_ver & 0xf000) >> 7) | (soc_ver & 0xf) - yields 0x01 for this SoC
version instead of the 0x21 the wcn3990 formula gives, so the driver asks
for a crbtfw01.tlv / crnv01.bin pair that is not this chip's firmware.
Bluetooth still came up, but on the wrong images; with the right ones the
controller also reports a different SCO buffer layout (240:4 rather than
60:8).

Every other board in tree, including the other sm7150 (google-sunfish),
uses qcom,wcn3990-bt.
---
 arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/sm7150-xiaomi-common.dtsi | 9 ++++++++-
 1 file changed, 8 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/sm7150-xiaomi-common.dtsi b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/sm7150-xiaomi-common.dtsi
index cc8f53a9f..adbf3c0fb 100644
--- a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/sm7150-xiaomi-common.dtsi
+++ b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/sm7150-xiaomi-common.dtsi
@@ -954,7 +954,14 @@ &uart3 {
 	status = "okay";
 
 	bluetooth: bluetooth {
-		compatible = "qcom,wcn3998-bt";
+		/*
+		 * The chip is a WCN3990: it reports ROM version 0x0201 and the
+		 * factory BTFM partition ships crbtfw21.tlv / crnv21.bin for it.
+		 * Declaring it as a wcn3998 picks a different rom_ver formula in
+		 * btqca.c ((soc_ver & 0xf000) >> 7 instead of (soc_ver & 0xf00) >> 4),
+		 * which asks for the nonexistent-for-this-chip "01" firmware pair.
+		 */
+		compatible = "qcom,wcn3990-bt";
 
 		vddio-supply = <&vreg_pmu_io>;
 		vddxo-supply = <&vreg_pmu_xo>;
